{
  "description": "EXPERIMENT (2026-11-24, owner: what the RTX 3080 Ti Laptop plays): e2e_fg_neural_13 with a 1248x1120 eye (50 % of the 1760x1600 eye's pixels): does the neural run time fall with the pixels, and does frame generation hold the display rate? neural frame generation at x3 (the 1/3 rate): the fixed pattern's outputs at t = 1/3 and 2/3, where RIFE 4.4 places the content at the asked time; every generated output composed from the fields, 0 failures, the display rate held.",
  "topology": {
    "host": "builder",
    "client": "builder",
    "client_bind_ip": "127.0.0.2",
